WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.650
Time for audience questions submitted throughout
the week, uh, by the audience.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.650
Let me know what you want

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.650
need to address on the show.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:11.110
First question is, Hey David, is Bernie's
anti endorsement list a good idea or will

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.110
it backfire?

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.630
So let me tell you what this is.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:18.320
First, Bernie Sanders put out a list, not
of people who have endorsed him, but if people

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.789
who have said don't vote for Bernie Sanders,
uh, this is a list of a bunch of prominent

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.199
billionaires.

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:27.099
There are Wall Street bankers on the list.

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:30.859
There are some big corporate CEOs who have
said, Bernie's a disaster.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:31.859
Don't vote Bernie.

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:33.719
Bernie's policies are terrible.

00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:38.550
So this could be both the, you know, the question
is, is it a good idea or will it backfire?

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.359
It can both be a good idea that backfires.

00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:44.820
I mean, that's sort of the idea of, of a backfire,
which is something that is a good idea.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.559
Ends up something ends up not going as planned.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:48.290
It ends up actually being counterproductive.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.719
So there's a bunch of people on this list
that are relatively notable.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.321
One that comes to mind to me is billionaire
cofounder of Home Depot, Kenneth Langan, who

00:00:57.321 --> 00:00:59.519
is a known big Trump booster.

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:02.739
A Disney CEO, Bob Iger is on the list.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:06.250
JP Morgan Chase, CEO, Jamie diamond is on
the list.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.210
So the idea here is the enemy of my enemy
is my friend.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:18.780
It's sort of the idea here, which is um, uh,
that if you see a or enemy of the of my enemy

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.790
is my friend in reverse sort of thing.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:28.790
The idea being if you see that a lot of these
big corporate multinational CEOs or whoever

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:34.729
don't like Bernie and you see the goals of
the, those same CEOs and billionaires as not

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:39.830
aligned with what you want, you might say
the fact that these CEOs and Wall Street bankers

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:45.840
don't like Bernie, uh, suggest to me that
Bernie does have my best interest in Bernie's

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.789
Po in mind and Bernie's policies would be
what's best for me and I am going to support

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:54.110
Bernie because these people don't like Bernie.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.530
It's a perfectly fine and reasonable idea.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:01.640
Uh, I think that the risk is of being couched
as being against rich people.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:06.810
And this is also a thing where, is it a badge
of honor or is it not a badge of honor?

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.879
Joe Biden famously a couple of weeks ago was
caught saying to a group of big donors, listen,

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:14.190
I don't think we should really hurt the rich.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.820
I don't think you're bad people.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.350
I'm not going after you.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.810
Nothing is substantively going to change for
you.

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.269
If I become president of the United States.

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:25.260
We're going to deal with some things sort
of around the edges and that's going to be

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.260
it.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.260
Bernie's taking a different approach.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:32.081
Bernie is saying, oh no, I am going to change
things for a lot of these big corporate CEO's

00:02:32.081 --> 00:02:33.709
and for Wall Street bankers.

00:02:33.709 --> 00:02:35.959
He's outlined some of the policies that would
do that.

00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:40.519
Raising taxes on the rich financial transactions,
taxes that would eat away at some of the Wall

00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:44.489
Street profits in order to take that money
and use it for useful social programs and

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:47.340
other kinds of economically stimulative spending.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.800
And the idea is that's good stuff.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.900
Bernie is saying things aren't going to be
so good for these corporate CEOs and bankers.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.880
That makes me like Bernie and I'm going to
vote for him.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.220
Now here's my bottom line opinion on this.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.510
I think it doesn't matter.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:01.510
Okay.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.900
I don't think endorsements matter very much
and in the same way, I don't think anti endorsements

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.180
very, very matter very much.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.610
It's fine that Bernie did this.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:15.269
It's possible that it will have some net positive
benefit to be perfectly frank, I just don't

00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:20.129
think many voters are either going to vote
for Bernie or not on the basis of whether

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:24.580
the home depot CEO Likes Bernie or doesn't
like Bern.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.590
I just don't think it matters.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:32.120
I truly don't, and there has been over time
more and more consensus that endorsements

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.840
really do not matter that much other than
there are some really specific things that

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.040
make a difference.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:44.500
Sitting presidents going around and saying,
I endorse x candidate and they are who should

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.340
take over for me and I'm going to aggressively
campaign for them.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.880
There is still the idea that that matters
didn't work out for Hillary Clinton with Barack

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.900
Obama, but in general there's the idea that
that can make a difference.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.470
Celebrity endorsements not really moving the
needle.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.540
Big political endorsements doesn't really
seem to make much of a difference.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.920
So I actually find myself thinking that it's
fine for Bernie to do this.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:13.470
There is a small enclave of the electorate
that may be influenced by this big picture.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.630
I don't think it's going to do much more for
him one way or the other.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.630
Let me know what you think.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:22.600
If you disagree with me, if you think that
Bernie's anti endorsement list will move the

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.260
needle in some way, could be for the better,
could be for the worst.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.260
Uh, let me know.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:27.720
I want to hear from you.

